#!/usr/bin/env xetal
# The LaTeX of an integral, from the same reading as its value: the
# bounds as written, the body, and d with the variable (a Greek
# letter's name as its command); nested, the inner variable's d first.
"e:" u_se< "Equations"
"L = \\int_{0}^{1} \\exp(\\tau) \\, d\\tau"
"L = \\int_{0}^{\\pi} \\sin(x) \\, dx"
"F_{t} = \\int_{0}^{2} \\exp(-\\tau) \\, \\exp(t - \\tau) \\, d\\tau"
"L = \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{x} x \\, y \\, dy \\, dx"
# A Greek letter's name as the result is its command too, capitals
# included (Phi, Sigma), with its subscript.
"\\Phi = \\frac{1}{2} + \\left(\\int_{0}^{x} \\frac{\\exp(-\\frac{u^{2}}{2})}{\\sqrt{2 \\, \\pi}} \\, du\\right)"
"\\sigma_{i} = \\sqrt{V_{i}}"
"\\Delta = \\alpha - \\beta"

